meta {
  name: Verify email (dev) — spend a token copied from the log
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/verify-email
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "token": "tlj1mQ1rNQjsNUS-YwDVU8TlTdoagH6acQf0zEOl5ZM"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 204
}

docs {
  There is no UI for this yet and email isn't wired up (docs/BACKEND.md), so in
  dev/QA the token only ever shows up in stdout as an
  `auth.verification.issued` JSON log line
  (src/server/services/accounts.ts:103-123) — that branch is the one place
  allowed to print a live credential, and only outside production.
  
  To use this request: grab the `token` field off that log line for the
  account you just signed up, set it as the `verificationToken` var on this
  request or in the environment, then Send. A 204 means the account is
  activated and can log in.
}
